  "reason": "The only completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) yielded a low accuracy of 48.5%, giving us a weak RNA baseline. The most critical uncertainty at this stage is whether the image modality carries useful predictive signal at all—if it does, multimodal fusion becomes a high-value direction; if it does not, we should concentrate remaining budget on improving RNA representations. Config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the cleanest single-variable comparison to the RNA baseline: it swaps modality while keeping profile setting (singleprofile) and encoder complexity (standard pretrained CNN) comparable. This isolates the effect of information source without confounding changes in aggregation, fusion, or encoder sophistication. With 8 experiments left, resolving whether image is a viable modality is the highest-information experiment before committing budget to multimodal or advanced-encoder configurations."
}

